From: 5sick <213179368+5sick@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: Optionally use the xdg-desktop-portal file chooser.

If HKCU\Software\Wine\FileDialog "HostFileChooser" is "Y", IFileDialog::Show()
(IFileOpenDialog / IFileSaveDialog without custom controls) and
GetOpenFileNameW() / GetSaveFileNameW() (without hooks or templates) ask
org.freedesktop.portal.FileChooser over the session bus (libdbus is loaded
at runtime by a new comdlg32 unixlib) and return the picked files. The
Windows filters, the initial folder and file name, multiple selection and
folder picking are passed on; the parent is given as "x11:<XID>".

Picked Unix paths below the target of a known folder that is a symlink in
the prefix (Downloads, Documents, ...) are returned through that folder.
Other folders the prefix can't reach (e.g. without a Z: drive) are linked
into C:\Linux\ (a symlink per picked folder, reused and kept so remembered
paths stay valid) and returned through that link, for opening, saving and
folder picking alike. Only if linking fails, files to open are copied to
%TEMP%\host-files\. If no portal is available, Wine's own dialog is shown.
---
